is in his second year of training as a  metal worker  he's doing his training at a vocational  center in berlin's kreitzberg district  he was sent here by germany's employment  agency  at the job center they told me this  place would give me a chance  and that i should take it it made me  want to really try hard  and go higher and higher  one of the top priorities is to restore  the trainee's confidence  many have dropped out of school or  applied for numerous jobs without  success  the items argan some say they're not  ready for training  others say they can't be taught we show  that isn't true if you make an effort  with this group  you can help them you can motivate them  and then they succeed  the center trains around 450 people at a  time  for occupations ranging from chef to  hairdresser or florist  social workers are on hand to support  the trainees and the center offers extra  german courses  many of the instructors are themselves  not native germans  like kevin moore from the u.s but only  german is spoken in the kitchen  outstanding as a foreigner i know this  can sometimes be difficult but that's  just one thing we all have to go through  you learn to express yourself in german  that's when land  of the londish bracket is also driven  some projections suggest that half of  young people in germany will soon come  from a migrant background  today the center's focus on immigrant  youth is something of an exception  but staff here are convinced that that  will change as this growing group  becomes ever more important  for the german labor market  you
 

